==== Installation via CFE web (http) server ====

**Note**: The RESET button doesn't work in this router for entering CFE failsafe. We will use the serial port TX-RX shortcircuit trick, otherwise a serial TTL adapter is required.

  * Set a **static IP** on your computer, use 192.168.1.35 (or any compatible), and connect the ethernet cable to the router.
  * Unplug the router's power cord
  * Shortcircuit TX and RX [[#Serial|serial pins]] (this will simulate keyboard buttons pressing on the serial port; ugly but it should work)
  * Plug the router's power cord and wait 3 or more seconds 
  * Remove the TX-RX shortcircuit.
    * You'll know it worked if, on boot, the first LED stays red
  * Browse to ''%%http://192.168.1.1%%'', you should see this screen:\\ {{:media:doc:cfe63xx_web-upgrade.png?400|}}
    * Note: the default address may be ''%%192.168.0.1%%'' instead, depending on the firmware version. If this is the case, you'll have to set your static IP to something like 192.168.0.35, and navigate to ''%%http://192.168.0.1%%'' which will redirect you to the screen shown above, which will be at ''%%http://192.168.0.1%%/upload.htm'' or equivalent
  * Send the new firmware and wait some minutes until the firmware upgrade finish. 
    * If you get an "illegal file" error, use the ...sysupgrade.bin file instead of the ...factory.chk file
  * ssh / telnet  to 192.168.1.1 and set a root password, or browse to ''%%http://192.168.1.1%%'' if LuCI is installed.

It's also possible to attach a [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial|serial]] console (serial TTL cable adapter required). Press any key at the console when starting up the router.


